# PART 2 — THE SAME SESSION, RE-RENDERED

Input identical to the previous run: `/slow Build an SOP for screening inbound supplier invoices...`

## Turn 1

```
[ACTIVE_SESSION]

[STRUCTURAL DIAGNOSIS]
Settled:  nothing yet — first pass.
Open:     matching logic, exception routing, quality standard, reviewer, assessment
          format, self-checks, analyst authority.
Reading:  this SOP issues pass/hold/escalate determinations, so three things must be
          stated before any determination is possible: what variance is acceptable, where
          each exception goes, and what makes an assessment wrong.

[QUESTIONS]

Q1. Variance tolerance
    What counts as within tolerance when the invoice and the PO line disagree?
    If skipped: halts every pass and hold determination at runtime until supplied.

  A  A percentage of the PO line value            → give the %
  B  A flat currency amount                       → give the amount
  C  Whichever of a percentage or flat is greater → give both
  D  Separate rules for price and for quantity    → give each

  Add "in" or "out" for an invoice sitting exactly on the threshold.

Q2. What makes an assessment wrong  (proposal)
    Selecting ratifies it as your standard. Any combination.
    If skipped: halts the run — this SOP issues determinations and cannot run without a
    stated failure condition.

  A  Evidential reconciliation — fails if a stated variance figure does not reconcile to
     the PO line cited
  B  Record existence — fails if the assessment cites a PO or GRN that does not exist
  C  Exception completeness — fails if an exception present in the data is absent from the
     assessment
  D  Duplicate check recorded — fails if the assessment does not record the duplicate
     check outcome
  E  None of these — I'll state my own

Q3. Where each exception goes
    Mark each H (hold) or E (escalate).
    If skipped: halts determinations on any invoice hitting an unmapped condition.

  a  duplicate suspected                     d  vendor not in vendor master
  b  no PO reference, or PO not found         e  variance outside tolerance
  c  goods-receipt note missing

  Reply like: "3: aE bE cH dE eH"

Reply "1B", or several: "1B 2A 3C".  Type your own answer instead of any letter.
"skip 2" defers one question.

[OTHER ACTIONS AVAILABLE]
  Compile now      -> open blockers become runtime halts; refinements take the defaults shown.
  Skip a question  -> "skip 2". That item only; the rest continue.
  Switch to fast   -> compile immediately, no further questions.
```

Note Q1 carries no numbers. Nothing in the input named a tolerance, so every option is a Form option. Note Q3 collapses what was four separate questions across two turns into five keystrokes, because hold and escalate are the user's own vocabulary — Settled options, legitimately.

