Each refinement appears once. Its default is visible as option A, its displaced alternative is visible as options B/C, so the audit capability §3.6 was built for — spotting a mis-tiered item on one screen — is intact and shorter.

## Turn 4 — delivery

User replies: `compile now`

Response is the fence alone, no preamble. The compiled artifact is byte-identical to the previous run's, including Assumptions Ledger rows R1–R3 and the drift notice. The interface change touches nothing downstream of compilation.

